00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.570
gives me access to
everything that I've created

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:17.400
so far in the Python space.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:21.170
And so I can go ahead
and use that object

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.600
to do something like this.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.650
So I grab some code
from my cheat sheet,

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.760
place it in this chunk.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:36.000
I'm essentially taking the
Python model predictions

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.955
and plotting them with ggplot2.

00:16:37.955 --> 00:16:39.330
And you can see
a little bit here

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:41.250
why our model fit is so bad.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.700
It's because we're not capturing
